## Why This Is Asked
Drift detection ensures model reliability and safe fallbacks in production scoring.

## Key Concepts
- Drift detection across model_version switches
- Telemetry fields: drift_flag, drift_reason, score_change_pct, last_model_version, last_score
- Fallback routing and drift alerts
- Observability and basic tests for drift, isolation, and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
function checkDrift(currentScore, lastScore, lastModelVersion, currentModelVersion, threshold=0.15){
  const drift = Math.abs(currentScore - lastScore);
  const versionChanged = currentModelVersion !== lastModelVersion;
  const driftFlag = drift > threshold || versionChanged;
  const driftReason = versionChanged ? 'model_version_change' : (drift > threshold ? 'score_change' : 'none');
  const scoreChangePct = lastScore ? ((currentScore - lastScore) / Math.abs(lastScore)) * 100 : 0;
  return { driftFlag, driftReason, scoreChangePct };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you store per-user drift telemetry at scale while preserving privacy?
- How would you tune the threshold and ensure safe fallbacks during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design a privacy-preserving ABAC layer that controls access to encrypted CCA score shares without revealing plaintext data. It tests understanding of dynamic admin access, revocation mechanisms, auditability, and system design at scale.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC attributes: tenant_id, region, role, expiry
- Token-based access without decryption
- Immutable audit logs with tamper-evident provenance
- Key management with per-tenant keys
- Revocation and expiry propagation

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePolicy(attrs, action) {
  const now = Date.now();

  if (attrs.expiry < now) return { allowed: false, reason: 'expired' };
  if (!attrs.tenant_id || !attrs.region) return { allowed: false, reason: 'missing attributes' };

  const policy = getPolicy(attrs.policy_id);
  if (!policy) return { allowed: false, reason: 'policy not found' };

  const regionMatch = policy.regions.includes(attrs.region);
  const roleMatch = policy.roles.includes(attrs.role);

  return { allowed: regionMatch && roleMatch, reason: regionMatch && roleMatch ? 'ok' : 'attribute mismatch' };
}

function revokeAccess(policyId, reason) {
  const policy = getPolicy(policyId);
  policy.revoked = true;
  policy.revocationReason = reason;
  publishRevocationEvent(policyId);
}
```

